brrPersonal dictionary data notice

The brrPersonal corpus-derived frequency seed is generated from PHINC (Parallel Hinglish Social
Media Code-Mixed Corpus for Machine Translation), curated by the Lingo Research Group at IIT
Gandhinagar. PHINC contains Romanized Hindi-English sentences paired with human English
translations and is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).

Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/LingoIITGN/PHINC
Pinned source revision: 44b5471df75e508b9d6fcdbcc93df04bb1e84056
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Paper: Vivek Srivastava and Mayank Singh, “PHINC: A Parallel Hinglish Social Media Code-Mixed
Corpus for Machine Translation,” W-NUT 2020, https://aclanthology.org/2020.wnut-1.7/

Modification: the build-time generator tokenizes only the Romanized Hinglish column, compares
counts with the paired English translations, removes common English function words, keeps terms
seen at least twice, caps the corpus-derived lexicon at 6,000 entries, and maps counts to the
existing decoder's native frequency field. A small owner-requested rules list adds valid-only
slang/profanity entries with emoji shortcuts. The source corpus is not bundled in the APK.
This bundled seed is a dated baseline, not a claim to represent every current regional trend.

No user-typed text, clipboard content, or learning history is included in the generated asset.
Personal learning remains in the app's existing local UserHistoryDictionary.

Optional private English speech recognition assets (one-time opt-in APK only)

The one-time brrBoard offline-voice bootstrap APK may bundle an ONNX export of
NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 110M English recognition weights, under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0). Attribution: NVIDIA Corporation, Parakeet TDT-CTC
110M English ASR (transducer head), https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m . The pinned
four-file export used by this project is mirrored by the DictateKeyboard model
release at https://github.com/DevEmperor/DictateKeyboard/releases/tag/whisper-models-v1 .
Its source hashes and sizes appear in tools/offline-voice-model.lock.
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . The source model is
quantized/exported; no model training or automatic retraining is performed.

The sherpa-onnx runtime is authored by the k2-fsa contributors and distributed
under Apache License 2.0: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx . brrBoard pins
release v2.0.2 at build time. These speech assets are absent from the ordinary
small Obtainium APK except the necessary speech runtime binaries.

